//! The refusals of direct imports. A listed name is a public item of its
//! module, and one that clashes with a name the file already has is refused,
//! naming both: an item of the module, the name of an imported module, a name
//! of another list and a name listed twice. A module is imported once, with its
//! list or without one. A name that no list holds stays behind the name of its
//! module, and a listed function is no function of a type of this module.

